@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+Analysis only, production a653b6c (3fac677 changes documentation only), ATL 5b14f2d.
+All generated artifacts, tool temporary files, packages and SDK files stay inside
+this worktree; the explicitly supplied ATL clone is read-only. No credentials.
+Apply docs/reviews/free-analysis-diag.patch only temporarily. It reuses the
+2026-11-22 diagnostics and adds PP token names, hidden-friend/C-linkage/literal
+metadata, association provenance and actual reverse potential-effect visits.
+No retention rule is changed.
+
+Use TMPDIR=$PWD/.checks/free/tmp throughout; mkdir -p that path and
+.checks/trim/tmp measurements/trim. Download the public release archive
+https://github.com/jcg9129/cpp-distill/releases/download/llvm-23.1.5-1/llvm-sdk-23.1.5-1-linux-arm64.tar.xz
+and sibling SHA256SUMS to .checks/free/. Verify SHA-256 before extracting to
+.checks/free/sdk (archive has a sdk/ top directory). Expected:
+5ca712f18c710592a8fa89758246a6b6cbdbd16c1fbd5f12c7f5bcdf35fe06de
+
+Under ulimit -v 5700000, timeout 120 cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
+ -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release '-DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE=-O1 -DNDEBUG'
+ -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++
+ -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=-fuse-ld=lld
+ -DDISTILL_LLVM_DIR=$PWD/.checks/free/sdk/sdk/lib/cmake/llvm
+Then timeout 900 cmake --build build --parallel 2.
+Run the six focused CTest suites listed in the review with timeout 240,
+ctest --timeout 120 -j2. Build-baseline.py (timeout 400) builds an unmodified
+HEAD extractor separately, with the same compile/link flags; it uses only one
+compiler job, keeps production sources in place and makes no policy change.
+Build helpers artifacts.cpp and .checks/trim/replay.cpp using timeout 120,
+clang++ -std=c++20 -O1 -Isrc <source> build/libdistill_core.a -pthread -o <output>.
+Name executables .checks/free/artifacts and .checks/trim/replay respectively.
+Delete the SDK extraction and archive after these builds/tests.
+
+Cross packages: timeout 600 python3 .checks/trim/acquire-cross.py installs
+checksum-verified compiler/runtime/binutils/QEMU packages into .checks/trim/cross.
+Then timeout 300 python3 .checks/free/acquire13.py adds the five GCC 13 compiler
+and development-header packages (each verified against public Ubuntu indexes).
+Use .checks/free/g++13, chmod +x. GCC 13 is necessary here: the original GCC 15
+-O2 setup cannot satisfy the new captured FLT_EVAL_METHOD facts and demotes the
+geometry conditions. Do not waive refusals. No GCC 15 trial output enters results.
+
+Measurement stages, sequential, at most two ATL examples per stage:
+  timeout 1800 python3 .checks/trim/sweep.py
+While that runs, continue-analysis.py may inspect finished sidecars and update
+the review; it does not compile/run examples. Or after sweep completion run
+analyze.py then report.py. Progress records are partial, never extrapolated.
+  timeout 300 python3 .checks/trim/replay-run.py
+  timeout 600 python3 .checks/free/check.py
+
+The extractor excludes actual resolved references, compiler used/referenced
+flags, standalone root/pins and main, as the earlier method. Raw and PP identifier
+witnesses feed strict/relaxed simultaneous fixpoints. Production effect visits
+are read from diag.effects.jsonl, not inferred solely from first-reason reports.
+Byte ownership is mapped through diag.render.json into actual out.cpp; compact
+owned-byte weights use production compactWhitespace and checked copy spans.
+After all examples finish, run refine-local.py, enrich.py and legacy-close.py
+before candidate checks. This includes local comparator units inside an unused
+free function, traces retention provenance, and records lexical-only totals before
+the separate potential-effect barrier. Then run check.py --top15, replay-run.py,
+audit.py and report.py.
+
+Raw/recomputed results live in measurements/trim/*/free-analysis.json;
+measurements/trim/free-summary.json contains totals. Report.py regenerates the partial/final tables and appends hazards.md plus
+observed validation results once all 126 examples have been analyzed.
+
+Save this diagnostic patch before restoring all changed production .cpp files
+and deleting src/core/prune/trim_diag.h. Only the review and patch remain tracked
+changes. No commit or push.
