+++ b/.checks/free/report.py
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+import pathlib,json,collections,datetime
+R=pathlib.Path.cwd();O=R/'measurements/trim';P=R/'docs/reviews/2026-11-24-free-function-analysis.md'
+rs=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in sorted(O.glob('*/free-analysis.json'))];done=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in O.glob('*/summary.json')]
+ds=[dict(d,example=r['name']) for r in rs for d in r['pool']];total=sum(r['bytes'] for r in rs);compact=sum(r['compactBytes'] for r in rs)
+def stats(rows):return f"{len(rows):,} | {sum(d['bytes'] for d in rows):,} | {sum(d['compact'] for d in rows):,}"
+def table(rows):return '\n'.join(rows)+'\n'
+def grouped(rows):
+ out={}
+ for d in rows:
+  key=(d['location'],d['name']);v=out.setdefault(key,dict(location=key[0],name=key[1],bytes=0,compact=0,count=0,examples=set(),rules=collections.Counter(),reason=collections.Counter(),witnesses=[]))
+  v['bytes']+=d['bytes'];v['compact']+=d['compact'];v['count']+=1;v['examples'].add(d['example']);reason=d['productionReason'];chain=d.get('retentionChain',[])
+  if len(chain)>1:reason+=' ← '+chain[1]['label']
+  v['reason'][reason]+=1
+  for rule in d['productionRules']:v['rules'][rule]+=1
+  v['witnesses']+=d.get('witnesses',[])
+ return sorted(out.values(),key=lambda d:(-d['bytes'],d['location'],d['name']))
+def esc(s):return s.replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
+groups={g:[d for d in ds if d['group']==g] for g in ['G1','G2','G3','G4','blocked c/d']}
+text=f'''<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
+# Free functions and hidden friends: candidate-rule analysis
+
+2026-11-24. Analysis only. Production base `a653b6c`; checked-out `3fac677` differs only in documentation. Read-only ATL `5b14f2d` (126 examples). No production policy change, commit or push.
+
+**Progress: {len(done)}/126 generated, {len(rs)}/126 analyzed; {sum(bool(r.get('sample')) for r in done)}/{len(done)} standalone sample checks pass.** Updated {datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).strftime('%H:%M:%S UTC')}. {'Final corpus totals.' if len(rs)==126 else 'Partial totals only; remaining examples are not extrapolated.'}
+
+## Measurement and method
+
+Reuses [the earlier free-function analysis](2026-11-22-trim-analysis.md#free-functions-and-hidden-friend-candidates) and its diagnostic patch. CSES `cses-gcc13-cpp23`, C++23, `-O2 --strip-comments --no-line-markers`, default A11/A12, following `ci/atl-sweep/sweep.sh`. Compiler: relocated x86_64 GCC 13.4, ARM64-hosted; standard-library headers are this compiler's headers, not a CSES GCC 13 capture. All inputs are read-only. Two examples maximum run concurrently; generation/compile/run caps 240/120/30 seconds, generation and compilation address-space cap 2,500,000 KiB. SDK LLVM 23.1.5 ARM64, release-SHA256SUMS verified: `5ca712f18c710592a8fa89758246a6b6cbdbd16c1fbd5f12c7f5bcdf35fe06de`; worktree-local download/extraction. Build `-O1 -DNDEBUG`, Clang 22.1.8, LLD, `-j2`, 5,700,000 KiB virtual-memory cap, hard configure/build caps 120/900 seconds. All six focused CTest suites pass (`unit`, `embedded_members`, `prune_extract_cases`, `prune_extract_models`, `member_pruning`, `member_review`). The SDK archive and extraction were deleted after the diagnostic/baseline builds and tests.
+
+The reused GCC 15.2 setup initially reproduced geometry flat fallbacks: its C++23 `-O2` checking configuration has no matching scanned standard-macro facts, so satisfaction demotes `FLT_EVAL_METHOD`. Those trial outputs are isolated in ignored `measurements/trim-gcc15/` and excluded here. GCC 13.4 matches the captured GCC-13 standard-macro input scope (`gcc-13@8255e82cc53970e5`); the complete measurement sweep was restarted with it. This is a compiler-configuration correction, with no gate waiver or policy modification.
+
+Counts are written declaration **occurrences across examples**, not unique header definitions. The initial pool excludes `main`, standalone root/pinned functions, any actual kept resolved reference (including unevaluated references and references from reached system entities), and any compiler used/referenced flag, conservatively including residual flags from discarded code. Template instances merge flags into their written declaration. Function-template headers, attributes and terminators belong to declarations; lambdas/function-local declarations do not become free-function candidates. Hidden friends are carved out of kept structural records. Function-local declarations belong to their enclosing written free declaration. Current main separately extracts three local comparator operators inside `locations_of` (`geometry/point_location.hpp:570`); the adapted group includes them, adding 309 nlm / 282 compact bytes, and removes the complete function. They are local member bodies, not non-member operator candidates under (a).
+
+The renderer copy map maps immutable input bytes to the actual nlm artifact; bytes absent from the artifact count zero. Compact counts map those same owned bytes through **production** `compactWhitespace`; the diagnostic checks exact output equality and the complete token/directive invariant. This is owned-byte attribution, excluding surrounding indentation, line breaks or renderer separators outside the declaration. Total nlm output: **{total:,} B**; compact: **{compact:,} B**. Whole-artifact deletion gains can differ slightly because separators/trivia survive or disappear.
+
+Starting with the whole pool, a simultaneous greatest-deletion fixpoint restores a declaration whenever its identifier name occurs outside the deletion set in retained raw tokens **or** the user preprocessed token stream. Both include uninstantiated bodies, signatures/defaults, constraints, macro definitions and arguments; strings/comments are excluded. A strict run additionally keeps operators, conversions, literal operators, guides, `main`, C-linkage and ADL-listed names. A relaxed run omits only these (a) exclusions. Production's actual reverse potential-effect traversal is recorded separately; any candidate in an effect-reachable aggregate or root/pin is excluded. Thus G1 satisfies the sketch within the existing A6/A7/A11 and preprocessing contracts; this is analysis, not a cross-library formal proof.
+
+## Recomputed pool
+
+| Partition | Declarations | Owned nlm B | Owned compact B |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+'''
+for g in groups:text+=f"| {g} | {stats(groups[g])} |\n"
+text+=f"| **Initial pool** | **{len(ds):,}** | **{sum(d['bytes'] for d in ds):,}** | **{sum(d['compact'] for d in ds):,}** |\n"
+if rs and all('legacyClosed' in r for r in rs):
+ legacy={k:sum(r['legacyClosed'][k] for r in rs) for k in ['declarations','nlm','compact']}
+ ec={k:sum(r['effectClosed'][k] for r in rs) for k in ['declarations','nlm','compact']}
+ text+=f"\nComparable lexical-only closure (before c/d): **{legacy['declarations']:,} declarations / {legacy['nlm']:,} nlm B / {legacy['compact']:,} compact B**. Of these, **{ec['declarations']:,} / {ec['nlm']:,} nlm B / {ec['compact']:,} compact B** are rejected by c/d. G1 is **{100*sum(d['bytes'] for d in groups['G1'])/legacy['nlm']:.2f}%** of this recomputed lexical-only nlm pool. The other c/d-rejected declarations also have external name witnesses.\n"
+text+='''
+G1 is the strict candidate gain. G2 consists of (a)-protected declarations in the relaxed lexical closure. G4 consists of ordinary helpers removed in the relaxed closure but kept by the strict one; their only remaining name users are within G2/G4. G3 is rejected even by the relaxed closure because identifiers remain elsewhere. These rows are disjoint; G1+G2+G4 is the lexical pool after the additional (c)/(d) barriers. The `blocked c/d` row is necessary: the four requested labels do not cover a declaration rejected by potential effects but not by (a) or (b). These bytes are not silently charged to G2 or G3. The earlier 185-declaration / 102,265-byte pool was lexical-only, so a fully comparable count must also include effect-rejected declarations that pass lexical closure; the comparable count is given above. G2 and G4 describe a hypothetical deletion group with the (a) barrier waived; a G2 owner can name a G4 helper.
+
+A hidden friend is **not by itself excluded by (a)**. The G2 hidden-friend rows below identify the actual reason (operator or ADL name).
+
+| G2 exclusion | Declarations | nlm B | compact B |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+'''
+for why in ['operator','hidden friend operator','ADL-listed name','hidden friend ADL name','other']:text+=f"| {why} | {stats([d for d in groups['G2'] if d['exclusionA']==why])} |\n"
+text+='\nG3 witness categories below are overlapping: one declaration can have both a same-name overload and a requires-expression witness.\n\n| External witness category | Declarations with witness | nlm B | compact B |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n'
+for kind in ['same-name declaration/overload','kept body/signature (including uninstantiated)','macro','requires-clause','coincidental member/local/parameter','kept structural/declaration text']:
+ rows=[d for d in groups['G3'] if any(w['kind']==kind for w in d.get('witnesses',[]))]
+ text+=f"| {kind} | {stats(rows)} |\n"
+for g in ['G1','G2','G3','G4','blocked c/d']:
+ text+=f'\n## {g}: top 15 written declarations\n\n| Source declaration | Occurrences | nlm B | compact B | Current reason / external witness |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n'
+ for d in grouped(groups[g])[:15]:
+  reason='; '.join(f'{a} ({n})' for a,n in d['reason'].most_common())
+  if d['witnesses']:
+   kinds=collections.Counter(w['kind'] for w in d['witnesses']);w=d['witnesses'][0]
+   reason='; '.join(kinds)+f"; e.g. `{w['location']}`: `{w['text']}`"
+  text+=f"| `{d['location']}` `{esc(d['name'])}` | {d['count']} | {d['bytes']:,} | {d['compact']:,} | {esc(reason)} |\n"
+text+='\n## G1 current-rule totals\n\nThese are mutually exclusive first retention reasons, not extra gains. `Name rule` is production lexical closure; association is the explicit keep rule 3, under the requested “other” category.\n\n| Current production rule | Declarations | nlm B | compact B |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n'
+reasonGroups=collections.defaultdict(list)
+for d in groups['G1']:
+ reason=d['productionReason']
+ key='Name rule / lexical closure' if reason.startswith('name:') else 'Family aggregation' if reason=='family aggregation' else 'Other: signature/type association (rule 3)' if reason.startswith('associated with') else 'AST closure' if reason.startswith('AST:') else 'Dependent-name closure' if reason.startswith('dependent name:') else reason
+ reasonGroups[key].append(d)
+for key in ['Name rule / lexical closure','Family aggregation','Other: signature/type association (rule 3)','AST closure','Dependent-name closure','A6','Potential effects','Root/pin']:
+ text+=f"| {key} | {stats(reasonGroups.get(key,[]))} |\n"
+text+='\n## G1: why every declaration remains today\n\nThe recorded reason is production’s first retention cause; aggregation and structural ownership can supply additional independent obligations. This complete source-declaration inventory groups repeated example occurrences.\n\n| Declaration | Occurrences | nlm B | compact B | Production rule | Exact first reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n'
+for d in grouped(groups['G1']):text+=f"| `{d['location']}` `{esc(d['name'])}` | {d['count']} | {d['bytes']:,} | {d['compact']:,} | {'; '.join(d['rules'])} | {esc('; '.join(f'{a} ({n})' for a,n in d['reason'].most_common()))} |\n"
+text+='\n## Hazards and validation\n\n'
+if len(rs)==126:
+ text+=(R/'.checks/free/hazards.md').read_text()+'\n'
+ checks=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in O.glob('*/g1-check.json')]
+ replays=[json.loads(p.read_text()) for p in O.glob('*/replay.json')]
+ passed=sum(c.get('passCheck',False) for c in checks);replayPass=sum(c.get('compare')==0 for c in replays)
+ unique={ (d['location'],d['name']) for d in groups['G1'] }
+ checkedExamples={c['example'] for c in checks if c.get('passCheck')}
+ covered={(d['location'],d['name']) for d in groups['G1'] if d['example'] in checkedExamples}
+ text+=f"\nAll 126 baseline artifacts prune and pass standalone sample output. Production whitespace compaction and token/directive invariants pass for all 126 measured artifacts. G1 deletion artifacts: **{passed}/{len(checks)}** selected example checks pass, covering **{len(covered)}/{len(unique)}** distinct written G1 declarations (the 15 largest example groups plus additional source-declaration coverage). The compacted deletion artifacts compile at `-O2` and match samples; no claim of every target/library instantiation is made. Unmodified-production-extractor replay: **{replayPass}/{len(replays)}** model comparisons pass after sorting/deduplicating unordered graph edges; unordered-edge order does not change retention. Six focused CTest suites pass, as listed above.\n"
+ text+='\nRaw per-example declarations, complete retention chains, raw/preprocessed witnesses, actual effect visits, rendered/compact copy maps, counterfactuals and check results remain in ignored `measurements/trim/`. The diagnostic patch and reproduction commands are in [free-analysis-diag.patch](free-analysis-diag.patch). Production sources are restored; SDK archive/extraction deleted. Only this review and that patch remain as git changes; nothing was committed or pushed.\n'
+else:
+ text+='Hazard audit and additional validation are in progress; partial raw data is in ignored `measurements/trim/`.\n'
+g1=sum(d['bytes'] for d in groups['G1']);share=g1/total*100 if total else 0
+text+=f'\n## Verdict\n\nThe strict candidate rule removes **{g1:,} owned nlm bytes ({share:.3f}% of {total:,} output bytes)** in the {len(rs)} analyzed examples. '
+if len(rs)==126:
+ text+='It looks worth building as a narrow namespace-function refinement: all measured G1 gain comes from namespace functions and their internal bodies, and the largest example (`delaunay-quick`) loses 48,861 owned bytes. The main change is to type association and the family/lexical closure it seeds; this corpus supplies no reason to weaken A6, non-member operator protection or potential-effect barriers, and no additional gain from ordinary hidden friends.\n'
+else:text+='This remains a partial result; no final worth-building judgment yet.\n'
+
+P.write_text(text)
+summary=dict(examples=len(rs),total=total,compact=compact,groups={g:dict(declarations=len(v),nlm=sum(d['bytes'] for d in v),compact=sum(d['compact'] for d in v)) for g,v in groups.items()},g1Share=share)
+(R/'measurements/trim/free-summary.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary,indent=2));print(json.dumps(summary),flush=True)
